.TH SWAYDESK-NOTIFD 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.2.1" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-notifd \- notification daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-notifd
.br
.B swaydesk\-notifd
\-\-headless
.SH DESCRIPTION
Owns org.freedesktop.Notifications on the session bus: it shows the notification toasts and keeps the list for the notification center and the Waybar icon, which talk to it through a control interface on the same bus name. Nothing is written to disk: the list ends with the process.
.PP
The session runs it under the name sway\-notifd (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-notifd); the process name is sway\-notifd too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run without windows, for the tests.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language, accent color, GTK and icon themes, folder color, file manager, weather location and holidays.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notify\-send (1),
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR swaydesk\-notifications (1),
.BR swaydesk\-notifications\-popup (1)
